-- Capability probe for upstream's cooperative per-leaf bounding-box reduction.
-- Required execution: independent groups reduce 32 lanes together; later leaf
-- traversal needs the same group to share a queue across loop iterations.
-- Failure to look for: each map lane serially reduces all 32 input elements,
-- or compilation rejects the nested reduction. Correct numbers alone do not
-- establish the cooperative execution needed for upstream parity.
-- Confirmed with installed compiler dated 2026-10-08 21:11 EDT: one 64-thread
-- map kernel, serial per-lane sum, no workgroup storage or barriers.
-- Same scheduling observed with installed compiler dated 2026-10-20 17:08 EDT.
-- This is a scheduling observation, not by itself a compiler defect: an inner
-- reduction may deliberately be serial when outer parallelism is sufficient.
-- wyn build fluid-simulation/test/repro_cooperative_leaf.wyn -o /tmp/cooperative-leaf.spv
-- spirv-dis /tmp/cooperative-leaf.spv -o /tmp/cooperative-leaf.spvasm
-- With input xs=[0..127], expect [496,1520,2544,3568].
entry reproduce(xs: []i32) []i32 =
  map(|leaf| reduce(|a,b| a+b,0i32,xs[leaf*32..(leaf+1)*32]),0i32..<(length(xs)/32))
